# Licences

Calliopa is two bodies of software under two licences. This file says which is which.
Neither licence covers the other's half.

## The extensions — Apache License 2.0

The interface shell, the settings extension, `calliopa-base` and `calliopa-extension`:
everything shipped as source in this repository and materialised into the graph.

Use, modify, fork and redistribute on Apache-2.0 terms. Full text in **`LICENSE-APACHE`**.

Rename before you redistribute: Apache-2.0 grants no trademark rights, and neither does
anything else here.

## The Calliopa Core — Calliopa Core Licence

The software published as the Calliopa release binaries: the bootstrap runtime, the
Calliopa-Cypher Gateway, the kernel, and the migration and seed tooling.

Proprietary. Free to run, for any purpose including commercial work, for one instance with one
distinguishable user. Not open source, not modifiable, not redistributable. Full text in
**`LICENSE-CORE.md`**.

## Third-party software — not distributed here

The compose file and its build recipes reference images published by other people. Docker
pulls them from their publishers to your machine, under their own licences. They are not part of Calliopa. See
`THIRD-PARTY.md` and `LICENSE-CORE.md` Section 7.

---

Calliopa is not open source. Its interface and its extensions are.
